  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You are given a permutation PPP of NNN integers from 111 to NNN.\n\nThe weight of a subarray [L,R][L, R][L,R] (1≤L≤R≤N)(1\\le L \\le R \\le N)(1≤L≤R≤N) is defined as ∣i−j∣|i - j|∣i−j∣ where iii denotes the index of the **maximum** element and jjj denotes the index of the **minimum** element in the subarray [L,R][L,R][L,R].\n\nFind the **sum** of the weights of **all** subarrays of the given permutation.\n\nNote that, ∣X∣|X|∣X∣ denotes the absolute value of a number XXX. For example, ∣−4∣=4|-4| = 4∣−4∣=4 and ∣7∣=7|7| = 7∣7∣=7.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line contains an integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases. The TTT test cases then follow:\nThe first line of each test case contains an integer NNN, denoting the length of the permutation.\nThe second line of each test case contains NNN space-separated integers P1,P2,…,PNP_1,P_2,\\ldots,P_NP1​,P2​,…,PN​, denoting the elements of the permutation.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output the **sum** of the weights of all subarrays of the given permutation.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1051 \\leq T \\leq 10^51≤T≤105",
      "1≤N≤5⋅1051 \\leq N \\leq 5\\cdot 10^51≤N≤5⋅105",
      "1≤Pi≤N1 \\leq P_i \\leq N1≤Pi​≤N and Pi≠PjP_i \\neq P_jPi​=Pj​ for i≠ji \\neq ji=j",
      "Sum of NNN over all test cases does not exceed 5⋅1055\\cdot 10^55⋅105."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "3\n3\n3 2 1\n4\n1 4 3 2\n7\n1 7 4 5 3 2 6",
        "output": "4\n7\n31",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest case 111:\n\nThe weights of the subarrays [1,1],[2,2],[3,3][1,1],[2,2],[3,3][1,1],[2,2],[3,3] are 000 as i=ji=ji=j in all these subarrays.\nSubarray [L,R]=[1,2][L,R] = [1,2][L,R]=[1,2] has weight 111 as i=1i=1i=1 and j=2j=2j=2: ∣1−2∣=1|1 - 2| =1∣1−2∣=1.\nSubarray [L,R]=[2,3][L,R] = [2,3][L,R]=[2,3] has weight 111 as i=2i=2i=2 and j=3j=3j=3: ∣2−3∣=1|2 - 3| =1∣2−3∣=1.\nSubarray [L,R]=[1,3][L,R] = [1,3][L,R]=[1,3] has weight 222 as i=1i=1i=1 and j=3j=3j=3: ∣1−3∣=2|1 - 3| =2∣1−3∣=2.\n\nSum of weights is 1+1+2=41+1+2=41+1+2=4.\nTest case 222:\n\nThe weights of the subarrays [1,1],[2,2],[3,3],[4,4][1,1],[2,2],[3,3],[4,4][1,1],[2,2],[3,3],[4,4] are 000 as i=ji = ji=j in all these subarrays.\nSubarray [L,R]=[1,2][L,R] = [1,2][L,R]=[1,2] has weight 111 as i=2i=2i=2 and j=1j=1j=1: ∣2−1∣=1|2 - 1| =1∣2−1∣=1.\nSubarray [L,R]=[2,3][L,R] = [2,3][L,R]=[2,3] has weight 111 as i=2i=2i=2 and j=3j=3j=3: ∣2−3∣=1|2 - 3| =1∣2−3∣=1.\nSubarray [L,R]=[3,4][L,R] = [3,4][L,R]=[3,4] has weight 111 as i=3i=3i=3 and j=4j=4j=4: ∣3−4∣=1|3 - 4| =1∣3−4∣=1.\nSubarray [L,R]=[1,3][L,R] = [1,3][L,R]=[1,3] has weight 111 as i=2i=2i=2 and j=1j=1j=1: ∣2−1∣=1|2 - 1| =1∣2−1∣=1.\nSubarray [L,R]=[2,4][L,R] = [2,4][L,R]=[2,4] has weight 222 as i=2i=2i=2 and j=4j=4j=4: ∣2−4∣=2|2 - 4| =2∣2−4∣=2.\nSubarray [L,R]=[1,4][L,R] = [1,4][L,R]=[1,4] has weight 111 as i=2i=2i=2 and j=1j=1j=1: ∣2−1∣=1|2 - 1| =1∣2−1∣=1.\n\nSum of weights is 1+1+1+1+2+1=71+1+1+1+2+1=71+1+1+1+2+1=7."
      }
    ]
